.TH THUMTOO-BENCH 1 "2026-09-16" "thumtoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thumtoo-bench \- cold-cache phase timing for thumtoo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thumtoo-bench
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
\fIPATH\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Benchmark thumtoo cold-cache phases on files or archives. Each phase uses a
fresh stats window; overall wall time is also reported. Default cache root is
under
.B thumtoo-bench
and is wiped each run unless .B \-\-keep\-cache is set. .B \-\-json emits machine-readable phase timings.
.PP
Typical phases: size probe, optional soft ladder, optional tile pyramid or
single-cell request. See
.B \-\-help
for options (
.BR \-\-jobs ,
.BR \-\-ladder ,
.BR \-\-tiles ,
.BR \-\-tile\-cell ,
\&...).
.SH OUTPUT
By default a phase table followed by the statistics of each phase is printed.
.B \-\-csv
prints one row per phase plus a total row (add
.B \-\-no\-header
to append to an existing file).
.B \-\-json
prints one document; every phase carries its numbers as
.I counters
next to the formatted
.IR stats .
Warnings and errors go to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No readable image was found in the given paths, or the run failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thumtoo (7),
.BR thumtoo-prepare (1),
.BR thumtoo-status (1)
